:: S: Depart from Apesai [storylet unfinished] {"position":"4600,2850","size":"100,100"}
{=

(storylet: when
$place's sublocation is "Apesai Wharf"
)

(metadata:
"title", "Depart from Apesai",
"cardDesc", "Ferries-for-hire flock the wharf, waiting to take those with the coins into mainland Askava.",
"img", "https://fallenlondon.wiki/w/images/3/3b/Shipilaltun.png",
"devNote", [Implement multi-check gates for the Navveh and Zirab options. Also, add item.licenseAdventure to the game],
)

$cssColumnParent[

$cssColumnChild[
	$cssBox[
    	($funcImage: (passage:)'s img)
         $cssBoxItem[''(print: (passage:)'s title )''<br>(print: (passage:)'s cardDesc)]
    ]
]

$cssColumnChild[

<!--roll which sailor you deal with today; there is no need for a global var, since I can just re-evaluate $dice in the next passage-->
(set: _whichSailor to "genericSailor1")
(cond:
    $dice <= 33, [(set: _whichSailor to "genericSailor2")],
    $dice <= 67, [(set: _whichSailor to "genericSailor3")],
    [(set: _whichSailor to "genericSailor1")],
)

<!--enchant speaker lines-->
($funcNPCSpeakManual: _whichSailor)

<!--line shorthand-->
(set: _line to (hook: _whichSailor + "Line"))


<!--main content-->

<!--greetings-->
(cond:
_whichSailor is "genericSailor1", [{
_line["You there, you with the clueless face! Looking for a ship to the mainland?"] a large woman in salt-stained linen hails you down.
<br>
Behind her is an old cutter that has seen better days, but that is precisely the mark of quality: worse ships will not sail if they are in such a condition.
<br>
_line["No point in browsing; we all charge a standard guild price here,"] she grins, showing teeth stained red-and-black. _line["Where are ya headed?"]
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor2", [{
_line["Ho, traveler! Yes, well met. Are you looking for a ship to the mainland?"] a man approaches you. He wears a quilted vest, arms bare and tattooed. _line["There's still space on our ship. We set sail today."]
<br>
He gestures at a large dromon with sweeping, fin-like sails. Smaller merchant ships often moonlight as coastal ferries while waiting for their shipments to arrive.
<br>
_line["My captain takes guild price like any other. Where are you bound?"]
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor3", [{
_line["My, what fortune for us to have met. Come, traveler. Are you looking for a way into the mainland?"] A man with fire-red hair and beard, clad in silk and gold, approaches you. _line["We just so happen to have a few spare cabins left. Come and see the //real// Askava."]
<br>
You can smell the new paint from here. Behind him is a fairly large vessel, where passengers are leaning over the deck's railing, taking in the sight from up high.
<br>
_line["It is a fine way to travel, is it not? Don't worry, we ask only for the standard guild price,"] he rubs his ringed hands together. _line["So, where should our journey take us?"]
}],
)
<br>
$cssDesc[Ferries from Apesai can go to every major ports of the Nurrah Coastlands, which include ''Rokhab'', ''Navveh'', and ''Zirab''.]
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\"Rokhab.\"", "Rokhab",
    "<!--B-->\"Navveh.\"", "Navveh",
    "<!--C-->\"Zirab.\"", "Zirab",
    "<!--D-->\"Never mind. I'm not interested right now.\"", "neverMind",
))
<br>


<!--Rokhab-->
[
(cond:
_whichSailor is "genericSailor1", [{
_line["Easy,"] she chuckles, _line["We'll be there in about three days, if the weather isn't being a pain in the ass."]
<br>
The Rokhab port is the closest to Apesai, so chances of things going awry is slim. After all, the Apesai-Rokhab route is the most used sea routes in the entirety of the dahak, and that puts your mind at ease somewhat.
<br>
_line["But I'll have to be a different sort of pain in your little behind and ask to see your entry permit first. Not collecting it or anything; just making sure."]
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor2", [{
_line["Ah, you make my life simple then,"] he smiles boardly, flashing a crystal tooth. _line["Port's about three days away, give or take, and the route should be trouble-free, weather not withstanding."]
<br>
The Rokhab port is the closest to Apesai, so any inclement weather should not interfere with the journey all that much. Further, the Apesai-Rokhab route is one of the most well-patrolled stretches of sea this side of Nurandah. You should be fine.
<br>
_line["Now, before we start discussing details, I must ask to see your entry permit first. Don't worry, I won't take it from you. The Rokhab guards will want to see it."]
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor3", [{
_line["How original,"] he rolls his eyes, disappointed. _line["I'm joking; we'll have to stop at Rokhab anyhow. Most of our passengers are headed there as well. Personally, I just don't like the smell."]
<br>
The Rokhab port is the closest to Apesai, and it is not surprising that it sees the most traffic going to and from, since Rokhab connects with the rest of the dahak, from which riches flows out.
<br>
_line["And now, it is my turn to do the unoriginal thing: Please show me your entry permit. Due diligence, you understand."]

}],
)
<br>
$cssDesc[Going to ''Rokhab'' requires an ''(print: (passage: "item.permitAskava")'s id)''($funcLogTip: "item.", "permitAskava").]

<!--papers check-->
(set: _havePapers to false)
(if: $char's player's inv contains "permitAskava")[(set: _havePapers to true)]

<!--set dialog option-->
(set: _say to "Um...")
(if: _havePapers is true)[(set: _say to "I have it right here.")]

<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\""+_say+"\"", "RokhabDone",
    "<!--B-->\"How about a different destination?\"", "differentDestination",
    "<!--C-->\"Never mind. I'm not interested right now.\"", "neverMind",
))
<br>
](Rokhab|


<!--RokhabDone-->
[
(cond:
_whichSailor is "genericSailor1", [{
She crosses her arms, waiting as you search your bag.
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor2", [{
He whistles, looking away, giving you the privacy to search your bag.
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor3", [{
He polishes a ring on his silk robe, waiting for you to search your bag. 
}],
)
<br>
---
<ol>
<li>($funcMultiCheckGate: "Show your permit.", "inv", (dm: "permitAskava", 1), false, 100, [], "Depart from Apesai 1a", "",)</li>
<br>
Actually...
<li>(link: "\"I'm interested in another destination.\"")[(t8n:"dissolve")(redirect: (passage:)'s name)]</li>
<li>(link: "\"Never mind. I'm not interested right now.\"")[$funcBack]</li>
</ol>
](RokhabDone|


<!--Navveh-->
[
(cond:
_whichSailor is "genericSailor1", [{
_line["The ruins?"] She raises her brows quizzically. _line["Why, are you some kind of Bone-digger? Treasure-hunter? Death-seeker? Ya know what, don't answer. Not my business."]
<br>
Most still recoil at the mention of Old Navveh. Once, it was the capital of Askava dahak. Now, the forest has reclaimed the once-grand city, and there is little left of its fame but superstitions. To be fair, it is not //all// superstition; the residual magical hazard is very real.
<br>
_line["What //is// my business whether that you're vetted. The whole Navveh rostak is declared 'culturally significant'; they're not letting just anyone in. Ya need to show me an entry permit and a Society's adventuring license. Those are the rules."]
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor2", [{
_line["Oh? You're interested in the ruins,"] he says, trying his best to hide his hesitation. _line["Shouldn't be a surprise. It is one of Askava's major attractions anyhow. Although, it is not the most pleasant waters to sail in."]
<br>
The quake that destroyed Old Navveh - the former capital of Askava dahak - has also disturbed the geology of its coastlines, raising up jagged rocks that make for a hazardous trip. Still, a small but steady number of adventurers go there every month, and a smaller number returns enviably rich, if they return at all.
<br>
_line["Ah, but we are professionals. We will sail, if you can show us the papers. Governor's rule is that, on top of an entry permit, you'll also need an adventuring license. The Traveler's Society issues those. It's for people's own good, you understand, to make sure their preparedness matches their bravado."]
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor3", [{
_line["The ruins? My, my, my, how //romantic//!"] The man covers his mouth in feigned shock. _line["The allure lost grandeur is one thing, but the //danger//. Oh! I'm getting goosebumps."]
<br>
The former capital of Askava dahak - Navveh - is one of the coastlands' major attractions. Every year, adventurers and scholars brave its magical (and natural) hazards, hoping to be enriched by the past, intellectually or materially. Few see their ambitions fulfilled, but the promise is enough for many.
<br>
_line["I envy the young, truly. If I were in charge of this land, I'd let all of you into Old Navveh, no questions asked. But alas, I am not, and so I must comply by the law and ask that you show me... ugh, a Society's adventuring license... on top of the standard entry permit, of course."]
}],
)
<br>
$cssDesc[Going to ''Navveh'' requires both an ''(print: (passage: "item.permitAskava")'s id)''($funcLogTip: "item.", "permitAskava") and an ''(print: (passage: "item.licenseAdventure")'s id)''($funcLogTip: "item.", "licenseAdventure").]

<!--papers check-->
(set: _havePapers to false)
(if: $char's player's inv contains "permitAskava" and it contains "licenseAdventure")[(set: _havePapers to true)]

<!--set dialog option-->
(set: _say to "Um...")
(if: _havePapers is true)[(set: _say to "I have it right here.")]

<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\""+_say+"\"", "NavvehDone",
    "<!--B-->\"How about a different destination?\"", "differentDestination",
    "<!--C-->\"Never mind. I'm not interested right now.\"", "neverMind",
))
<br>
](Navveh|


<!--NavvehDone-->
[
(cond:
_whichSailor is "genericSailor1", [{
She crosses her arms, waiting as you search your bag.
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor2", [{
He whistles, looking away, giving you the privacy to search your bag.
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor3", [{
He polishes a ring on his silk robe, waiting for you to search your bag. 
}],
)
<br>
---
<ol>
<li>($funcMultiCheckGate: "Show your papers.", "inv", (dm: "permitAskava", 1, "licenseAdventure", 1), false, 100, [], "Depart from Apesai 2a", "",)</li>
<br>
Actually...
<li>(link: "\"I'm interested in another destination.\"")[(t8n:"dissolve")(redirect: (passage:)'s name)]</li>
<li>(link: "\"Never mind. I'm not interested right now.\"")[$funcBack]</li>
</ol>
](NavvehDone|


<!--Zirab-->
[
(cond:
_whichSailor is "genericSailor1", [{
_line["Oh... Oh-ho-ho,"] she starts guffawing, as if you have just told her a brilliant joke. _line["Wait, really? What's in Zirab for //you//? Ya know what? Never mind, it's not my place to question a customer."]
<br>
Zirab rostak is largely fallow marshland and isolated holdings given to less-than-favored soldiers. In other words, exiles. People are hesitant to live there, let alone develop it. It is never clear if any given patch of wetland is Nurandah or Yavana, which makes any property a liability. That, and the mosquito-borne diseases.
<br>
_line["I'm only to do as I'm told. The governor requires that only Grand Exchange merchants are to sail there, to make sure the swamp-dwellers don't starve. But otherwise, most traffic is... heavily discouraged. Ya need to show me a trading license, on top of the usual entry permit."]
}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor2", [{
_line["Zirab? Please don't tell me..."] he trails off. _line["Yes, in fact, do //not// tell me. The less I know, the better."]
<br>
Zirab - a fallow marshland bordering Yavana to the south-east - is unfortunately known to being a smugglers' den. Its ambiguous status and hostile environment makes it unattractive to investors and settlers but a wonderful sanctuary for those looking to evade the governor's tight grip on trade.
<br>
These things are well-known, but the guards and navy are momentarily turning a blind eye. Anything that might be cosntrued as a territorial encroachment will threaten peace with Yavana. Askava already has the Kesh in the north to deal with.
<br>
_line["I only know that I must ask for a trading license, on top of the usual entry permit. Only Grand Exchange merchants are allowed to sail there, for the moment."]

}],

_whichSailor is "genericSailor3", [{
_line["Zirab? Don't you mean to say //Vayu//?"] The large man huffs, jiggling his golden knives. _line["Ah, but I shouldn't expect an imperial to know its //proper// name. Yes, we do sail to... ugh, //Zirab//."]
<br>
Zirab - also known as "Vayu" to the Yavanids - is the marshy part of the Nurrah Coastlands bordering Yavana to the south-east. Neither Yavana, Nurandah, Kesh, or even the native Askavans have ever openly fought over that land, since it is of little value to those who are prone to mosquito-born diseases, which is to say: everyone.
<br>
Most would rather live on Apesai island instead. After all, why fight over a piece of swampland while peaceful coexistence is possible in one of the biggest cities of the Nurrah Sea? All of this, your school has taught you.
<br>
_line["Your governor has decreed that only Grand Exchange traffic is allowed to land in the marshes. To save us some trouble later on, please show me your trading license, in addition to the usual entry permit."]
<br>
}],
)
<br>
$cssDesc[Going to ''Zirab'' requires both an ''(print: (passage: "item.permitAskava")'s id)''($funcLogTip: "item.", "permitAskava") and an ''(print: (passage: "item.licenseTrade")'s id)''($funcLogTip: "item.", "licenseTrade").]

<!--papers check-->
(set: _havePapers to false)
(if: $char's player's inv contains "permitAskava" and it contains "licenseTrade")[(set: _havePapers to true)]

<!--set dialog option-->
(set: _say to "Um...")
(if: _havePapers is true)[(set: _say to "I have it right here.")]

<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\""+_say+"\"", "ZirabDone",
    "<!--B-->\"How about a different destination?\"", "differentDestination",
    "<!--C-->\"Never mind. I'm not interested right now.\"", "neverMind",
))
<br>
](Zirab|


<!--ZirabDone-->
